Problem Statement



Rohan, a data scientist, has been tasked with processing a dataset for his team. To speed up sorting, he divides the dataset into smaller parts and sorts each part
  using Merge Sort, utilizing multithreading for parallel processing.



Your task is to implement a multi-threaded Merge Sort program that sorts the array efficiently. The array must be divided into 2 or more parts, each sorted concurrently 
  using separate threads. After sorting, merge all parts to produce a fully sorted array.

Input format :
First line: an integer n, the size of the array.



Second line: n space-separated integers representing the elements of the array.

Output format :
First line: "Sorted Array:"

Second line: n space-separated integers representing the sorted array.



Refer to the sample output for the formatting specifications.

Code constraints :
The given test cases fall under the following constraints:

2 ≤ n ≤ 12

-1 ≤ array elements ≤ 95

The array must be divided into min(4, n) parts, with at least 2 parts always used, each sorted concurrently using a separate thread.

Only Merge Sort should be used to sort the array.

Sample test cases :


      Input 1 :
          6
          12 5 8 1 9 3
      Output 1 :
          Sorted Array:
          1 3 5 8 9 12 

            
      Input 2 :
          8
          34 7 23 32 5 62 74 2
      Output 2 :
          Sorted Array:
          2 5 7 23 32 34 62 74 
